  "text_sample": "Your Page Title Sandstone&amp;co\u00ae Projects 06 Services 06 Studio Since 2010 Contact Say hello Overview Buy Sandstone Latest project Harbour hotel lounge Porvoo, Finland Helsinki Fredrikinkatu 34 00100 Helsinki Mon to Fri, 9 to 18 +358 00 000 0000 [email protected] LinkedIn Instagram Behance How we choose a dining chair You will sit on it every day for twenty years. Here is the short list of checks every chair has to pass before it reaches a client. Sofia Ramirez Senior interior designer Published 14 September 2025 A dining chair is the piece of furniture people touch most and think about least. We spend more time choosing them than almost anything else in a room. Sit for ten minutes Not ten seconds. A chair that feels fine in a showroom can dig into your back halfway through dinner. We sit through a full coffee in every chair we shortlist. Lift it with one hand If you cannot pull it out from the table with one hand, it will scratch the floor and nobody will use it. Light chairs get moved, and rooms with movable chairs get used. Look at the joints Good chairs are made to be repaired. We check how the legs meet the seat, whether parts can be replaced and whether the maker still offer",
